repository-code: 'https://github.com/Shanmuk4622/tyre-wear-alignment-cv'
abstract: >-
  A vision system for detailed inspection of a single automotive
  tyre using a low-mounted camera placed ahead of the wheel and
  directed at the visible tread surface. The system segments the
  tyre, tread crown, shoulders, grooves, ribs, sipes and tread-wear
  indicators; predicts ordinal wear severity, multi-label wear
  patterns, a localised wear heatmap and visible damage; and
  produces a calibrated screening estimate of single-wheel camber
  and individual toe with uncertainty. Multi-directional
  (photometric-stereo) illumination recovers surface normals so that
  groove and crack geometry is measurable on low-albedo rubber.
  Video frames are quality-gated, registered and fused into a
  partial unrolled tread map with explicit circumference-coverage
  reporting. Alignment is computed from calibrated analytic geometry
  with a learned residual correction rather than by direct
  image-to-angle regression. Every output carries a conformal
  prediction interval, and the system can return UNABLE_TO_MEASURE
  when image quality or geometry is insufficient.
